</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Antonini</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Continuous apomorphine infusion and neuropsychiatric disorders: a controlled study in patients with advanced Parkinson&#x02019;s disease</article-title><source>Neurol Sci</source><volume>24</volume><fpage>174</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14598073</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15-ndt-3-335"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Diamond</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Jankovic</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>The effect of deep brain stimulation on quality of life in movement disorders</article-title><source>J Neurol Neurosurg Psychiatry</source><volume>76</volume><fpage>1188</fpage><lpage>93</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16107348</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-ndt-3-335"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dodel</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Eggert</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Singer</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Costs of drug treatment in Parkinsons disease</article-title><source>Mov disord</source><volume>13</volume><fpage>249</fpage><lpage>54</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9539337</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17-ndt-3-335"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dodel</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Berger</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Oertel</surname><given-names>WH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Health-related quality of life and healthcare utilisation in patients with Parkinson&#x02019;s disease: i